      id: 1744969277934,
      title: 'Aggregation in MongoDB',
      content:
        '<h3>🧩 <strong>What is Aggregation in MongoDB?</strong></h3><p><br></p><p>Aggregation in MongoDB is a framework that allows you to perform advanced data processing and transformations on collections, similar to SQL\'s GROUP BY, JOIN, HAVING, etc.</p><p><br></p><p>It works through an aggregation pipeline, where data passes through multiple stages, and each stage transforms the data before passing it to the next.</p><p><br></p><p>Example:</p><p>Stage 1 ➝ Stage 2 ➝ Stage 3 ... ➝ Final Output</p><p><br></p><h3>🧪 <strong>Common Aggregation Stages (Operators)</strong></h3><p><br></p><p><img src="data:image/png;base64,"></p>',
      tags: [153, 126, 51],
